From: Alan Shearer
Subject: virtio_gpu accelerant: do not close clone fd twice

init_common(fd, true) sets is_clone. uninit_common() already closes the
device fd for clones. The clone_area failure path called uninit_common()
then fell through to close(fd) again.

Return after uninit_common() so only the init_common() failure path
closes the fd.

---
 src/add-ons/accelerants/virtio/accelerant.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/accelerants/virtio/accelerant.cpp b/src/add-ons/accelerants/virtio/accelerant.cpp
--- a/src/add-ons/accelerants/virtio/accelerant.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/accelerants/virtio/accelerant.cpp
@@ -128,6 +128,7 @@
 
 err2:
 	uninit_common();
+	return status;
 err1:
 	close(fd);
 	return status;
